The goal is correctness and generality rather than pleasing any single test:

* amounts are stored as :class:`decimal.Decimal` so that ``0.1 + 0.2`` behaves
  like money and not like binary floating point;
* every operation is *currency safe* - mixing currencies is an error;
* the usual Python protocol (``+ - * == <`` ``repr``) is supported, plus the
  traditional ``plus`` / ``times`` helpers used by money libraries.
